From 1dd87f341c530d598d54785a3ebb4752307eddfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:32:35 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 142/159] rule-set: a rule set closed while it reads a list
 stops reading it

A remote rule set checked its context before and after the parse of a
downloaded list, not during it: a box closed meanwhile (an in-process
reload: SIGHUP) let the parse of a big list run to the end beside the new
box, which downloads and parses its own.

The readers take the context of the rule set: the source format
(domainset.ReadSourceContext) looks at it every 4096 items, the build of
the trie every 4096 nodes, a binary set reads through a reader that ends
with the context, and the rules are made one at a time. Local rule sets
read so too.
